  "published": "2026-06-21T14:19:45.087Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.6.1\n      - Added PdfRequest.Compress (default true) + PdfRequestBuilder.WithCompression(bool): controls output PDF compression (maps to the editions' WithCompression(bool)). Legacy SkipPostProcessing / WithSkipPostProcessing() retained as the inverse for back-compat (builder deprecated).\n      - Added PdfRequest.ViewportWidth / ViewportHeight + PdfRequestBuilder.WithViewportSize(width[, height]): sets the render viewport; a tall height triggers IntersectionObserver lazy images without scrolling.\n      - Added PdfRequest.ForceEagerImages + PdfRequestBuilder.WithEagerImages(): forces lazy-loaded images (loading=\"lazy\" and data-src/data-srcset) to load before rendering.\n      - All additive and honoured by both the CobaltPDF (Chromium) and CobaltPDF.WebKit 1.6.0 editions. Object-initializer construction is unchanged.\n\n      v1.6.0\n      - Added a fluent builder for PdfRequest, mirroring the CobaltEngine fluent API: PdfRequest.ForUrl(url) / PdfRequest.ForHtml(html), chained .WithPaperFormat/.WithMargins/.WithHeader/.WithWatermark/.WithEncryption/.WithMetadata/.AddCookie/... then .Build(). PdfRequest.ToBuilder() adapts an existing instance. The fluent path produces an identical PdfRequest (and identical JSON) to the object-initializer style.",
